ename-eq-identity — two ENAMEs for the same entity are not EQ / EQUAL
====================================================================

Found: schms-parity 1.6.6, while smoke-testing the entity lifecycle.

Symptom
-------

In AutoCAD / BricsCAD two entity names that denote the SAME entity are
EQ (and EQUAL). In clautolisp each call that yields an ename mints a
FRESH wrapper, so neither EQ nor EQUAL holds:

  $ clautolisp --host mock -x '(progn
      (setq e (entmakex (list (cons 0 "LINE")
                              (cons 10 (list 0 0 0)) (cons 11 (list 1 1 0)))))
      (princ (if (eq e (entlast)) "EQ" "NOTEQ")))'
  NOTEQ            ; AutoCAD/BricsCAD print EQ

This breaks the common portable idioms
  (if (eq ename (car sel)) ...)
  (if (eq (ssname ss i) target) ...)
  (member ename list-of-enames)      ; EQ-based

Cause
-----

clautolisp.autolisp-mock-host::handle->ename (entity-api.lisp) does
  (make-autolisp-ename :value handle)
on every call — entget, entlast, entnext, handent, ssname, entmakex all
build a new struct for the same handle. autolisp-ename equality is
struct identity, so same-entity enames differ.

Fix sketch
----------

Intern enames per handle so the same handle yields the same (EQ) ename
object within a session/drawing: a handle->ename cache on the drawing
(or the host), populated by handle->ename and invalidated with the
drawing. Alternatively, give autolisp-ename value-based EQL/EQUAL
semantics in the runtime's equality builtins (EQ must stay identity, so
the interning approach is the faithful one — vendor EQ is true).

Scope / risk
------------

Cross-cuts every ename producer. Out of scope for the schms-parity
entity-CRUD pass (which is about entity data, not ename identity), so
deferred and filed here. Add a portable probe assertion
(eq (entlast) (entlast)) once fixed. Listed in the Deferred section of
entity-mutation-parity.issue.

===========================================================================
RESOLUTION (2026-07-30) — clautolisp 1.7.3, interning approach.
===========================================================================

Fixed by interning enames per handle on the MockHost, so every producer
yields the same (EQ / EQUAL) ename object for a given handle within a
drawing — matching vendor AutoLISP, where EQ is true for two enames of
the same entity.

  - mock-host gained an ENAME-CACHE (handle-string -> autolisp-ename)
    plus ENAME-CACHE-DRAWING (the drawing the cache is valid for).
  - handle->ename now takes HOST, drains the cache when the active
    drawing identity changes (future multi-drawing sessions), and
    interns: same handle -> same object.
  - Every producer routes through it: the entget (-1 . ename) head
    (entity->al-view), entlast, entnext, entmakex/%host-add-entity,
    entmod, handent, ssname (selection-api), tblobjname
    (table-record->ename), namedobjdict / dictsearch / dictnext /
    dictremove / dictobjname (dictionary-api). The two remaining direct
    make-autolisp-ename call sites (ssname, table-record->ename) were
    rerouted through handle->ename.

Verified (clautolisp --host mock):
  (eq (entlast) (entlast))          => T
  (eq e (entlast))                  => T   ; e from entmakex
  (eq e (entnext))                  => T
  (eq e (handent (cdr (assoc 5 (entget e))))) => T
  (eq e (ssname (ssget "X") 0))     => T
  (member e (list (entlast)))       => non-nil
  (equal e (entlast))               => T
  distinct entities: (eq a b)       => nil   ; interning does not conflate

Regression pins added to autolisp-mock-host/tests/entity-api-tests.lisp
(6 tests: entlast-eq-across-calls, entmakex-eq-to-entlast/entnext,
entget-head-eq, handent-eq, ssname-eq+member, distinct-not-eq). Mock-host
FiveAM suite 727 -> 737 checks, 100% pass; conformance corpus unchanged
(3666 pass / 218 fail); EQ stays struct identity (only interning changed).

CLOSED.
